# a5sf-p2-read — RED capture (BL-14 / P2-01, dated 2026-11-03, real UTC)

Host-free. No boot, no port, no DSH_HOME, no budget row. This file is the capture
taken BEFORE the package's laws could hold, not a re-run of the green state.

Three RED measurements, all real command output:

  RED 1  the gate's module does not exist (the file this package adds) — every arm is
         red with ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND, the "no gate at all" baseline.
  RED 2  mutation M1: the FOREIGN-COMMIT comparison in the gate is DELETED. The
         foreign-grant arm must go red; the other arms stay green (a targeted
         mutation, not a blanket breakage).
  RED 3  mutation M2: the pre-reservation EXHAUSTION refusal is DELETED. The
         exhausted-shared-ledger arm must go red.

Method: each mutation was applied to tests/world-factory/suites/150-a5sf-read.mjs, the
suite was run, then the module was restored from a saved copy. `orig sha` / `restored
sha` below must both equal the module's sha256 after this package's final edit
(11e2f3e597709d490172314ab1d92d7ef99cd469f877a5f5a68220135c8fbbf6). A capture is worthless if the file it measured is not the file shipped.

Mutation table (what was deleted -> which arm must red -> observed):

  M1  `if (String(headCommit) !== grant.boundCommit) { throw … GRANT_FOREIGN_COMMIT … }`
      -> arm 4 "a grant bound to ANOTHER commit refuses"            -> RED (1 failed)
  M2  `if (before.exhausted) { throw … GRANT_EXHAUSTED … }`
      -> arm 6 "an EXHAUSTED shared ledger refuses and leaves the
               ledger byte-identical"                               -> RED (1 failed)

